  "body": "### Description\r\n\r\nWith Synaps 0.99.5.2, running `hash_password` yields an `AttributeError` when accessing the `pepper` key of the `password_config` section, when it is empty.\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n- Install Synapse 0.99.5.2\r\n- Create a sample configuration file with `python -m synapse.app.homeserver --server-name example.com --config-path config.yaml --generate-config --report-stats=yes`\r\n- Run `hash_password -c /path/to/config.yaml`\r\n\r\n```\r\n$ hash_password -c /path/to/config.yaml \r\nTraceback (most recent call last):\r\n  File \"[…]/bin/hash_password\", line 56, in <module>\r\n    password_pepper = password_config.get(\"pepper\", password_pepper)\r\nAttributeError: 'NoneType' object has no attribute 'get'\r\n```\r\n\r\n`config.yaml` contains the default `password_config` stanza, i.e.:\r\n\r\n```yaml\r\npassword_config:\r\n   # Uncomment to disable password login\r\n   #\r\n   #enabled: false\r\n\r\n   # Uncomment and change to a secret random string for extra security.\r\n   # DO NOT CHANGE THIS AFTER INITIAL SETUP!\r\n   #\r\n   #pepper: \"EVEN_MORE_SECRET\"\r\n```\r\n\r\nPatching the line causing the error to this seems to avoid the issue:\r\n\r\n```python\r\n        password_config = config.get(\"password_config\", None) or {}\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Version information\r\n\r\n- **Homeserver**: (own, can use fresh example setup)\r\n- **Version**: 0.99.5.2\r\n- **Install method**: PIP\r\n- **Platform**: Debian GNU/Linux stable\r\n",
